      <div id="sutta">
  
        <h4 id="thig6.3" class="h1">Thig 6:3  Khemā</h4>
        <p><em>In <a href="../../SN/SN5_4.html">SN 5:4</a>, a variation of the verse attributed to Māra, and the first verse attributed here to Sister Khemā, are included in a poem attributed to Sister Vijayā (see <a href="thig6_8.html">Thig 6:8</a>). Sister Khema’s second verse is attributed to Sister Aḷavikā in <a href="../../SN/SN5_1.html">SN 5:1</a>. Her third verse also appears in <a href="thig7_2.html">Thig 7:2</a>; its first half, in <a href="../../SN/SN5_3.html">SN 5:3</a>.</em></p>
        <div class="verse">
          <p class="vspk">Māra:</p>
          <p>“You, a beautiful young woman;</p>
          <p>I, a young man, full of youth.</p>
          <p>Come, Khemā,</p>
          <p>let’s enjoy ourselves</p>
          <p class="v2">to the music of a five-piece band.”</p>
          <div class="verse-add">
          <p class="vspk">Khemā:</p>
          <p>“I’m disgusted, ashamed</p>
          <p>of this putrid body—</p>
          <p>disintegrating, dissolving.</p>
          <p class="v2">Sensual craving</p>
          <p class="v4">is rooted out.</p>
          </div><!--end verse-add-->
          <div class="verse-add">
          <p>Sensual pleasures</p>
          <p class="v2">are like swords &amp; spears;</p>
          <p>the aggregates,</p>
          <p class="v2">their executioner’s block.</p>
          <p>What you call <em>sensual delight</em></p>
          <p class="v2">is <em>no delight</em> for me.</p>
          </div><!--end verse-add-->
          <div class="verse-add">
          <p>Everywhere enjoyment</p>
          <p class="v2">is defeated;</p>
          <p>the mass of darkness,</p>
          <p class="v2">burst.</p>
          <p>So know,      Evil One,</p>
          <p>that you have been,</p>
          <p class="v4">End-maker,</p>
          <p class="v2">struck down.”</p>
          </div><!--end verse-add-->
        </div><!--end verse-->
          <p class="verse_stars">* * *</p>
        <div class="verse">
          <p>Paying homage to the zodiac stars,</p>
          <p>tending the fire in the forest,</p>
          <p>not knowing it as it actually was,</p>
          <p class="v2">fools, you conceived it</p>
          <p class="v2">as purity.</p>
          <p>Whereas I</p>
          <p class="v2">am one who pays homage</p>
          <p class="v2">to the One Self-awakened,</p>
          <p class="v2">the utmost man.</p>
          <p>I’m one who has done the Teacher’s bidding,</p>
          <p>entirely released</p>
          <p>from sufferings &amp; stress.</p>
        </div><!--end verse-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
